=== 1. estate_notifications: the two columns the case needed (archived_at, pinned) ===
 column_name |        data_type         | is_nullable |   default_value   
-------------+--------------------------+-------------+-------------------
 id          | uuid                     | NO          | gen_random_uuid()
 category    | text                     | NO          | 'general'::text
 read_at     | timestamp with time zone | YES         | -
 created_at  | timestamp with time zone | NO          | now()
 archived_at | timestamp with time zone | YES         | -
 pinned      | boolean                  | NO          | false
(6 rows)

=== 2. indexes on estate_notifications: active half, archived half, trigram search ===
            indexname            |                                                                                             indexdef                                                                                             
---------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 estate_notifications_pkey       | CREATE UNIQUE INDEX estate_notifications_pkey ON public.estate_notifications USING btree (id)
 idx_estate_notifications_user   | CREATE INDEX idx_estate_notifications_user ON public.estate_notifications USING btree (estate_id, user_id, created_at DESC)
 idx_notifications_search_trgm   | CREATE INDEX idx_notifications_search_trgm ON public.estate_notifications USING gin (((((COALESCE(title, ''::character varying))::text || ' '::text) || COALESCE(body, ''::text))) gin_trgm_ops)
 idx_notifications_unread        | CREATE INDEX idx_notifications_unread ON public.estate_notifications USING btree (user_id) WHERE (read_at IS NULL)
 idx_notifications_user          | CREATE INDEX idx_notifications_user ON public.estate_notifications USING btree (user_id, created_at DESC)
 idx_notifications_user_active   | CREATE INDEX idx_notifications_user_active ON public.estate_notifications USING btree (user_id, created_at DESC) WHERE (archived_at IS NULL)
 idx_notifications_user_archived | CREATE INDEX idx_notifications_user_archived ON public.estate_notifications USING btree (user_id, archived_at DESC) WHERE (archived_at IS NOT NULL)
(7 rows)

=== 3. pg_trgm availability decides whether search is indexed or a seq scan ===
 pg_trgm_installed 
-------------------
 t
