=== 4. the retention policy table: RLS on, defaults, and every CHECK ===
                relname                 | relrowsecurity 
----------------------------------------+----------------
 estate_notification_retention_policies | t
(1 row)

                        conname                        |                                                                                               definition                                                                                               
-------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 estate_notification_retention_policies_estate_id_fkey | FOREIGN KEY (estate_id) REFERENCES estates(id) ON DELETE CASCADE
 estate_notification_retention_policies_pkey           | PRIMARY KEY (estate_id)
 estate_nrp_archive_positive                           | CHECK ((archive_after_days > 0))
 estate_nrp_keep_categories_valid                      | CHECK ((keep_categories <@ ARRAY['general'::text, 'payment'::text, 'meeting'::text, 'election'::text, 'security'::text, 'maintenance'::text, 'facility'::text, 'announcement'::text, 'system'::text]))
 estate_nrp_purge_after_archive                        | CHECK (((purge_after_days IS NULL) OR (purge_after_days >= archive_after_days)))
 estate_nrp_purge_positive                             | CHECK (((purge_after_days IS NULL) OR (purge_after_days > 0)))
(6 rows)

    column_name     | is_nullable |              default_value              
--------------------+-------------+-----------------------------------------
 estate_id          | NO          | -
 enabled            | NO          | true
 archive_after_days | NO          | 90
 purge_after_days   | YES         | -
 keep_categories    | NO          | ARRAY['security'::text, 'system'::text]
 updated_by         | YES         | -
 updated_at         | NO          | now()
(7 rows)

                polname                | polcmd |   for_roles    
---------------------------------------+--------+----------------
 notification_retention_policy_service | *      | {service_role}
(1 row)

=== 5. the purge guard: a BEFORE DELETE trigger, enabled, on every delete path ===
                   tgname                   | tgtype | tgenabled |                                                                               definition                                                                                
--------------------------------------------+--------+-----------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 estate_notifications_block_purge_on_delete |     11 | O         | CREATE TRIGGER estate_notifications_block_purge_on_delete BEFORE DELETE ON public.estate_notifications FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION estate_notifications_block_purge()
(1 row)

